---
description: Google SEO Best Practices for Web Development
---

# Technical SEO
- Use semantic HTML elements (header, nav, main, section, article, footer) for better document structure
- Implement proper heading hierarchy (h1-h6) with only one h1 per page
- Add descriptive alt text to all images
- Ensure fast page load times (< 3 seconds) using performance optimization
- Make website mobile-friendly with responsive design
- Use HTTPS for secure connections
- Implement schema.org structured data markup for rich snippets
- Create an XML sitemap and submit to Google Search Console
- Create and maintain a robots.txt file

# Content SEO
- Include target keywords in title tags, meta descriptions, headings, and content
- Create unique meta descriptions (150-160 characters) for each page
- Create unique title tags (50-60 characters) for each page
- Ensure content is unique, valuable, and relevant to the user
- Maintain minimum content length of 300 words per page
- Use internal linking to connect related content
- Include outbound links to authoritative sources when appropriate

# Performance
- Optimize and compress images before uploading
- Use lazy loading for images and videos
- Minify CSS, JavaScript, and HTML
- Implement browser caching
- Use a Content Delivery Network (CDN) when possible
- Eliminate render-blocking resources
- Reduce server response time

# User Experience
- Make navigation intuitive and simple
- Ensure all interactive elements are accessible (WCAG compliance)
- Design for readability with appropriate font sizes and contrast
- Minimize intrusive interstitials and pop-ups
- Implement breadcrumb navigation on larger sites
- Show clear call-to-action buttons
- Ensure proper handling of 404 errors with custom pages

# Technical Implementation
- Implement canonical URLs to prevent duplicate content
- Use rel="nofollow" for external links when appropriate
- Add hreflang tags for multilingual websites
- Implement proper pagination with rel="next" and rel="prev"
- Use descriptive URLs with keywords when possible
- Implement Open Graph and Twitter card meta tags for social sharing
